7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
{"parentUuid":"87d1aa5f-b0a6-4093-8b5a-f4f01a4a1274","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"a0759a3f131ba1536","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019oNheYjN9mAGuTjtnDwZyN","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"_doc\": \"Every cross-cutting requirement from the brief has one owning skill that defines the obligation and reviews every other skill against it. 'obligation' is what each skill's SKILL.md must address in phase 2.\", \"concerns\": [{\"concern\": \"performance\", \"owner\": \"performance-architect\", \"obligation\": \"Declare budgets per tier, hot paths, and the benchmark that proves them.\"}, {\"concern\": \"memory usage\", \"owner\": \"memory-performance\", \"obligation\": \"Declare allocation strategy, memory tags, peak/steady budgets and OOM behavior (mechanisms by memory-allocators).\"}, {\"concern\": \"cache behavior\", \"owner\": \"cpu-performance\", \"obligation\": \"Declare data layouts of hot data and access patterns; justify pointer chasing.\"}, {\"concern\": \"concurrency\", \"owner\": \"concurrency-primitives\", \"obligation\": \"Declare shared state and synchronization; follow thread-safety annotation conventions.\"}, {\"concern\": \"latency\", \"owner\": \"frame-orchestration\", \"obligation\": \"Declare frame phase placement and latency contribution.\"}, {\"concern\": \"determinism\", \"owner\": \"determinism-replay\", \"obligation\": \"Declare the determinism level provided and how it is tested.\"}, {\"concern\": \"observability\", \"owner\": \"observability-telemetry\", \"obligation\": \"Declare trace zones, counters and logs; zero cost when compiled out.\"}, {\"concern\": \"debugging\", \"owner\": \"visual-debugging-tools\", \"obligation\": \"Declare debug visualizations, inspectors and console commands.\"}, {\"concern\": \"testing\", \"owner\": \"test-architect\", \"obligation\": \"Meet the test definition of done (unit, contract, integration, fuzz where untrusted).\"}, {\"concern\": \"scalability\", \"owner\": \"performance-architect\", \"obligation\": \"Declare behavior from the smallest to the largest configuration, scaling knobs, unit costs and asymptotic class per world-scale dimension; spatial replicas update in O(changes).\"}, {\"concern\": \"security\", \"owner\": \"security-engineering\", \"obligation\": \"Declare untrusted inputs and validation; follow the trust-boundary contract.\"}, {\"concern\": \"platform portability\", \"owner\": \"platform-architect\", \"obligation\": \"No platform code above the PAL; declare capability-tier behavior.\"}, {\"concern\": \"maintainability\", \"owner\": \"architecture-governance\", \"obligation\": \"Contracts documented, ADRs recorded, fitness functions pass.\"}, {\"concern\": \"tooling\", \"owner\": \"editor-architect\", \"obligation\": \"Declare authoring path, inspectors and editor integration; tool logic is domain-owned, the editor provides the host.\"}","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cf3cc9e5-30db-45d7-91d1-10b3d22f7279","timestamp":"2026-09-29T16:23:10.523Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"87d1aa5f-b0a6-4093-8b5a-f4f01a4a1274","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1","slug":"warm-pondering-kernighan"}
